{
  "id": "y9-algorithms-l6",
  "label": "9CT.01 L6: Selection - A Machine That Thinks",
  "steps": [
    {"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Sequence Retrieval","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l6_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Sequence Retrieval</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Quick recall from last lesson.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-a\">(a) What keyword starts every procedure call?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-b\">(b) In a sequence, why must you buy a seed before you plant it?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"title","label":"Selection: A Machine That Thinks","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithms and Data</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Selection: A Machine That Thinks</h2><p>Year 9, 9CT.01</p></div>"},
    {"id":"objectives","label":"Three Goals","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Three Goals</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Decide</h3><p>Use <code>IF ... THEN</code> so a line only runs when a condition is true.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Choose</h3><p>Use <code>ELSE</code> so the machine always does exactly one of two things.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Combine</h3><p>A machine that checks before it acts never gets stuck.</p></div></div>"},
    {"id":"direct-instruction","label":"IF / ELSE Syntax","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">IF / ELSE Syntax</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A sequence always runs every line. <strong>Selection</strong> lets a machine skip lines, or choose between two different ones.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF SeedCount(&quot;Carrot&quot;) &gt; 0 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Plant(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Buy(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Cambridge Pseudocode has no colon and no &quot;DO&quot; on an IF line.</li><li><code>SeedCount(...)</code> is a <strong>function</strong> - it gives back a value, so it is never written with CALL in front.</li><li>Only one branch ever runs: THEN if the condition is true, ELSE if it is false.</li><li>An IF block always ends with <code>ENDIF</code>.</li></ul>"},
    {"id":"worked-check","label":"Check: Which Branch Runs?","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l6_worked_check","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Which Branch Runs?</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Look at the sequence again.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF SeedCount(&quot;Carrot&quot;) &gt; 0 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Plant(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Buy(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-a\">(a) The farmer owns 0 Carrot seeds. Which branch runs?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-b\">(b) What exactly is the condition checking?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-worked-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"farmer-tutorial","label":"Machine Tutorial: Smart Auto-Farm","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y9-algorithms-l6-farmer-button","appId":"pseudocodefarmer","appQuery":"tutorial=smart-auto-farm","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Machine Tutorial: Smart Auto-Farm</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Open Pseudocode Farmer. It will take you straight into the Smart Auto-Farm tutorial - follow every step in order.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Complete when</h3><p>The tutorial panel says &quot;Tutorial complete&quot; and your machine is standing on the farm, choosing between planting and buying by itself.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-farmer-button\">Open Pseudocode Farmer</button></div>"},
    {"id":"scaffold-fill-blank","label":"Fill the Missing Piece","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l6-fill-blank","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l6_fill_blank","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Fill the Missing Piece</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Right now, nothing happens if the farmer does not already own a Potato seed.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF SeedCount(&quot;Potato&quot;) &gt; 0 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Plant(&quot;Potato&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-fill-blank-a\">What single line would you add, and where, so a Potato seed gets bought when there isn't one?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-fill-blank-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-fill-blank-a\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-fill-blank-button\">Check answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-fill-blank-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"independent-task","label":"Independent Task: Afford It?","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l6-independent","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l6_independent","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Independent Task: Afford It?</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Write your own IF/ELSE from scratch. No walkthrough this time - work out the condition yourself.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Requirement</h3><p>Write a sequence: if the farmer has 20 coins or more, buy a Tomato seed. Otherwise, buy a Potato seed instead, since it's cheaper.</p></div><div class=\"pseudocode-check\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-independent-code\"><strong>Your IF/ELSE</strong></label><textarea id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-independent-code\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-independent-code\" spellcheck=\"false\" rows=\"6\"></textarea><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-independent-check\">Check my answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-independent-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div></div>"},
    {"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Selection","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l6_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Selection</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-a\">(a) What instruction ends every IF block?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-b\">(b) What does ELSE let a machine do that a single IF cannot?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l6-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Next lesson: <strong>Iteration</strong> - making a machine repeat a known number of times.</p>"}
  ],
  "validators": {
    "y9_algorithms_l6_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*call\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Every procedure call starts with CALL."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*(?:own|have|need|before)).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"You cannot plant a seed you have not bought yet."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l6_worked_check":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*(?:else|buy)).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"With 0 seeds owned, the condition is false, so the ELSE branch runs."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*(?:seed|own|carrot|count)).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"It checks how many Carrot seeds the farmer currently owns."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l6_fill_blank":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*else)(?=.*buy).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Add an ELSE branch, between the Plant line and ENDIF, containing CALL Buy(\"Potato\")."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l6_independent":[{"suffix":"code","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"if\\s*money\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*>=\\s*20\\s*then[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*buy\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']tomato[\"']\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*?else[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*buy\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']potato[\"']\\s*\\)","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Check the threshold (20), which crop is bought when you have enough (Tomato), and which is bought otherwise (Potato)."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l6_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*endif\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Every IF block closes with ENDIF."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*(?:choose|decide|other|instead|both|two|guarantee)).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"ELSE guarantees exactly one of two actions always happens, not zero or two."}]
  }
}
